# Modbus Register Operations

## Essential Documentation
**ALWAYS** reference these files before implementing inverter communication:
- **[doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md](mdc:doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md)** - Complete protocol specification
- **[doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md)** - Read/write registers (0x03, 0x06, 0x10)
- **[doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md)** - Read-only registers (0x04)
- **[doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md](mdc:doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md)** - Quick reference guide

## Function Codes
- **0x03**: Read Hold Registers (multiple)
- **0x04**: Read Input Registers (multiple)
- **0x06**: Write Single Hold Register
- **0x10**: Write Multiple Hold Registers

## Critical Protocol Rules
- **Maximum Registers**: 40 registers per query
- **Group Boundaries**: Must start at 0, 40, 80, 120, 160, etc.
- **Cross-Group Queries**: Split into multiple queries if crossing boundaries
- **Example**: To read registers 38-40, use two queries: 38-39 and 40

## Data Format
- **Byte Order**: Little-endian
- **Register Width**: 2 bytes (16-bit)
- **16-bit Integers**: High and low byte order is reversed
- **32-bit Integers**: High and low word order is reversed, byte order within each word is reversed

## Common Register Groups
- **System State**: Registers 0-9 (input registers)
- **Power Monitoring**: Registers 10-19 (input registers)
- **Function Control**: Register 21 (hold register)
- **BMS Parameters**: Registers 81-106 (input registers)
- **Advanced Control**: Register 110 (hold register)

## Error Handling
- Implement proper CRC16 validation
- Handle communication timeouts
- Retry failed operations with exponential backoff
- Log all communication errors for debugging
